    <!-- Mahjong Solitaire: screen texts. -->
    <string name="mj_help_title">How to Play Mahjong Solitaire</string>
    <string name="mj_help_body">Clear the board by removing pairs of matching tiles. A tile can be removed only when it is free: nothing lies on top of it and its left or right side is open. Tap a free tile, then tap a second free tile that matches it.\n\nTiles match when they show the same suit and number, the same wind or the same dragon. Any flower matches any other flower, and any season matches any other season.\n\nBlocked tiles are dimmed and crossed with lines. If no pair is left, press Shuffle to re-deal the remaining tiles. Undo is unlimited. Hint shows a free pair with a dashed outline.\n\nYour best time is saved for each layout, but only for boards you finish without a hint or a shuffle. Every deal can be cleared, though a wrong pairing can leave you stuck.</string>
